c>Anas platyrhynchos</italic>)</article-title><source>Anim Genet</source><year>2000</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>233</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10895321</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Maak</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wimmers</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Weigend</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Neumann</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><article-title>Isolation and characterization of 18 microsatellites in the Peking duck (<italic>Anas platyrhynchos</italic>) and their application in other waterfowl species</article-title><source>Mol Ecol Notes</source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>224</fpage><lpage>227</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1471-8286.2003.00405.x</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>G-S</given-names></name><name><surname>Yao</surname><given-names>Y-G</given-names></name><name><surname>Qu</surname><given-names>K-X</given-names></name><name><surname>Ding</surname><given-names>Z-L</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Palanichamy</surname><given-names>Mg</given-names></name><name><surname>Duan</surname><given-names>Z-Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Y-S</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>Y-P</given-names></name><article-title>Population phylogenomic analysis of mitochondrial DNA in wild boars and domestic pigs revealed multiple domestication events in East Asia</article-title><source>Genome Biol</source><year>2007</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>R245</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/gb-2007-8-11-r245</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18021448</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><